description:
The column tally (task count) should sit at the very bottom of each column regardless of how many cards are in it. Currently it appears directly under the last card, and for empty columns it sits near the top.

## Root cause
The .column div is auto-sized by its content. .cards { flex: 1 } only pushes tally to the bottom if .column has a fixed height. Because bd-column is a grid item (in the .columns CSS grid in bd-epic-lane), its host element does not automatically stretch to fill the full grid cell height — it sizes to content instead.

## Fix
Add height: 100% to both :host and .column so the flex layout fills the full grid cell height (the grid already stretches all cells to the height of the tallest column via align-items: stretch).

In src/client/board/column.ts:

  :host {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--bd-mocha-surface, #313244);
  }
  :host(:last-child) {
    border-right: none;
  }
  .column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 3rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.625rem;
  }
  .cards { flex: 1; }

With height:100% on both, .cards expands to fill available vertical space and .tally is pinned to the bottom of every column.

## Tests
No new unit tests needed — CSS layout change. Run pnpm test for regressions. Verify visually with pnpm dev: empty columns should show the tally at the same vertical position as the bottom of the tallest column in the same epic row.

## Commit
git commit -m 'fix(ui): pin column tally to bottom via height 100%'

Wrap SSE state updates in document.startViewTransition() so the browser animates cards moving between columns when their status changes. Extract the logic into a testable exported function. Initial load skips the transition (no before-snapshot exists).

## What to change

### src/client/store/board-store.ts
Export a pure function before the class:

  export function applyStateUpdate(
    newState: BoardState,
    setter: (state: BoardState) => void,
  ): void {
    if ('startViewTransition' in document) {
      document.startViewTransition(() => setter(newState))
    } else {
      setter(newState)
    }
  }

In connectSSE(), replace:
  this.boardState = JSON.parse(e.data as string) as BoardState
with:
  const newState = JSON.parse(e.data as string) as BoardState
  applyStateUpdate(newState, (s) => { this.boardState = s })

loadInitialState() keeps direct assignment — no transition on first load.

### tests/unit/board-store.test.ts
Add imports: import { vi } from 'vitest' and import { applyStateUpdate } from '../../src/client/store/board-store.js'

Write tests first (TDD), confirm fail, then implement:

  describe('applyStateUpdate()', () => {
    it('calls setter directly when startViewTransition is unavailable', () => {
      const setter = vi.fn()
      const orig = (document as any).startViewTransition
      delete (document as any).startViewTransition
      applyStateUpdate(newState, setter)
      expect(setter).toHaveBeenCalledOnce()
      expect(setter).toHaveBeenCalledWith(newState)
      if (orig) (document as any).startViewTransition = orig
    })
    it('calls startViewTransition when available', () => {
      const setter = vi.fn()
      const mockVT = vi.fn((cb: () => void) => { cb(); return {} })
      ;(document as any).startViewTransition = mockVT
      applyStateUpdate(newState, setter)
      expect(mockVT).toHaveBeenCalledOnce()
      expect(setter).toHaveBeenCalledWith(newState)
      delete (document as any).startViewTransition
    })
    it('setter receives the exact state object passed in', () => {
      const setter = vi.fn()
      delete (document as any).startViewTransition
      applyStateUpdate(newState, setter)
      expect(setter.mock.calls[0][0]).toBe(newState)
    })
  })

Run: pnpm test && pnpm test:e2e — all pass.

## Commit
git commit -m 'feat(ui): View Transitions on SSE board state updates'
git push

## Context
Depends on beads-dashboard-zhg.5 (cards must have view-transition-name set for browser to animate them).
